From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pogo-bash <pogo-bash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:02:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 45/46] LibWeb: Permissions, Notification permission, Screen,
 ScreenOrientation and NetworkInformation as Chrome answers them

navigator.permissions and PermissionStatus are exposed (they were behind
[Experimental]). A query knows Chrome's permission names, answers each
one's state for an origin with no stored decision (granted where Chrome
grants without asking), reports Chrome's status names (camera is
"video_capture"), checks push's userVisibleOnly and fullscreen's
allowWithoutGesture, and rejects unknown or disabled names with
Chrome's messages. Nothing is granted without a prompt: outside test
mode a permission request is treated as dismissed (the caller hears
"denied", nothing is stored, the state stays "prompt").

Notification.permission and Notification.requestPermission() follow
the notifications permission ("default" while it is "prompt");
maxActions is 2.

Screen gets availLeft/availTop; the available area, color depth and
screen count can come from the page client. ScreenOrientation's type
and angle come from the client (else the screen's shape), lock()
rejects with Chrome's NotSupportedError message, unlock() does
nothing, and Screen::orientation_did_change() fires change.

NetworkInformation (navigator.connection): effectiveType, rtt,
downlink, saveData and onchange, values from the page client.

An AudioContext without a sampleRate option runs at the page client's
audio output rate (the default output device's, as in Chrome), not 44100.
